✅ COLUMN ALIASES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Aliases make result columns easier to read, especially when using functions or long
column names.

EXAMPLE 1: SIMPLE COLUMN ALIASES
────────────────────────────────
QUERY:
SELECT CustomerID AS ID, CustomerName AS Customer
FROM Customers;

OUTPUT:
┌────┬──────────────────────────┐
│ ID │ Customer                 │
├────┼──────────────────────────┤
│ 1  │ Alfreds Futterkiste      │
│ 2  │ Ana Trujillo Emparedados │
│ 3  │ Antonio Moreno Taquería  │
│ 4  │ Around the Horn          │
│ 5  │ Berglunds snabbköp       │
└────┴──────────────────────────┘

Rows affected: 5

EXPLANATION:
• The query output columns are renamed to ID and Customer.
• Aliases only affect the display, not the underlying table.


EXAMPLE 2: ALIASES WITH SPACES
────────────────────────────────
QUERY:
SELECT CustomerName AS Customer, ContactName AS "Contact Person"
FROM Customers;

OUTPUT:
┌──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────┐
│ Customer                 │ Contact Person      │
├──────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
│ Alfreds Futterkiste      │ Maria Anders        │
│ Ana Trujillo Emparedados │ Ana Trujillo        │
│ Antonio Moreno Taquería  │ Antonio Moreno      │
│ Around the Horn          │ Thomas Hardy        │
│ Berglunds snabbköp       │ Christina           │
└──────────────────────────┴─────────────────────┘

Rows affected: 5

EXPLANATION:
• Use quotes for aliases containing spaces or special characters.
• Single quotes also work depending on SQL mode: AS 'Contact Person'.


